{{see|Joe}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/dʒoʊ/}}, {{SAMPA|/dZoU/}}

===Etymology 1===
From the common man's name.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{informal}} A [[male]]; a [[guy]]; a [[fellow]].
#: ''I'm just an ordinary '''joe'''.''

===Etymology 2===
Unconfirmed.  Hypotheses include:
* From "Old Black Joe", the title of a popular [[w:Stephen Foster]] song
* From French ''chaud'' meaning hot

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{mainly|US|informal}} [[coffee|Coffee]].
#: ''Give me a cuppa '''joe'''.''

=====Related terms=====
* [[cup of joe]]

